[FINAL-TEXT] Ping works — 0% packet loss, RTT ~0.5-2.5 ms. BGP clean, routes correct both directions.

=== DIAGNOSIS ===
is_anomaly: false
faulty_devices: none
diagnosis_text:
The network is operating correctly. Direct investigation found no fault at any layer.

BGP session between router1 (AS 1, 193.10.11.1) and router2 (AS 2, 193.10.11.2) is fully established — both peers show `Established` state with uptime ~1m44s, each receiving exactly the expected prefix from the other. Router1's FIB contains `B>* 200.1.1.0/24 via 193.10.11.2 eth0` and router2's FIB contains `B>* 195.11.14.0/24 via 193.10.11.1 eth0`, meaning end-to-end routing is properly installed in both directions.

pc1 (195.11.14.2) has a working default route to its gateway 195.11.14.1 (router1 eth1). pc2 (200.1.1.2) has a working default route to 200.1.1.1 (router2 eth1). A live ping from pc1 to 200.1.1.2 completed with 4/4 packets received and 0% packet loss (RTT 0.5–2.6 ms), confirming full end-to-end reachability at the time of investigation.

Root cause: No fault exists — the network is healthy and pc1 can reach pc2 at 200.1.1.2 without issue.

Corrective action: None required. The issue reported in ticket #9001 may have been transient (e.g., BGP convergence in the ~1–2 minutes after lab startup before routes propagated) and has self-resolved. Advise the user to retry their application. If the symptom recurs, check BGP session stability over time and whether the FRR process on either router restarts.
=== END ===